From 83bdbd21ebd032503a7c10bc7b082a22d98ef292 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritvik <ritvik2014@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:23:41 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/38] lumen-glass v3: light/dark glass decided once, told to
 the client

Replaces the per-frame light/dark guess (it flickered as a pill expanded:
its sample points slid across the backdrop every frame). Now the capture
reads back the frosted backdrop's brightness behind each shape (5 pixels,
at most every 200 ms); each shape decides light/dark with hysteresis (on
above 0.56, off below 0.40) and a change must hold for two readings; the
glass crossfades over 300 ms. Clients at v3 get an 'appearance' event per
change so their text switches with the glass (full light then; v1/v2
clients keep light at 80% for white text).
---
 resources/lumen-glass-v1.xml                 |  18 ++-
 src/protocols/lumen_glass.rs                 |  20 +++-
 src/render_helpers/framebuffer_effect.rs     | 101 +++++++++++++++-
 src/render_helpers/liquid_glass.rs           | 116 ++++++++++++++++++-
 src/render_helpers/shaders/liquid_glass.frag |  23 ++--
 5 files changed, 250 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

